OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Sat 28 Nov to Mon 7 Dec
OL,6,FThrough the rest of November and into
OL,7,Fearly December, the UK will remain
OL,8,Funder the competing influence of high
OL,9,Fpressure extending across the country
OL,10,Ffrom the northeast and Atlantic
OL,11,Fweather systems attempting to arrive
OL,12,Ffrom the west or southwest. Western
OL,13,Fand southwestern parts of the UK are
OL,14,Flikely to see the most frequent and
OL,15,Fheaviest spells of rain. Conditions in
OL,16,Fthe north and east are likely to be
OL,17,Fdrier though still with some rain at
OL,18,Ftimes. This pattern means temperatures
OL,19,Fwill often be below average with any
OL,20,Fmilder interludes most probable in the
OL,21,Fsouthwest. Snow is also likely at
OL,22,Ftimes across parts of the UK, most
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Flikely over northern hills.
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16303
SC,0003
CT,20,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1795443551
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G3/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Mon 7 Dec to Mon 21 DecFThe
OL,6,Ftrack of low pressure systems will
OL,7,Flikely be further south than normal
OL,8,Fduring this period. This means that
OL,9,Frainfall will probably be focused
OL,10,Facross the south of the UK with a risk
OL,11,Fof stronger winds at times;
OL,12,Fconversely, higher pressure closer to
OL,13,Fthe north means drier and more settled
OL,14,Fconditions are more likely here.
OL,15,FTemperatures in the south will
OL,16,Fprobably be near normal or perhaps
OL,17,Fslightly above at times, with the
OL,18,Fnorth colder than normal, although
OL,19,Feither bias could extended to cover a
OL,20,Fwider area of the UK.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
